.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt EGGHEAD-TOOLS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm egghead-tools
.Nd inspect the agent tool catalog and configured MCP servers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm egghead tools
.Op Cm list
.Op Fl -agent Ar agent-id
.Op Fl -source Cm all | local | mcp
.Nm egghead tools mcp
.Op Cm list | available | show Ar name | who Ar name | remove Ar name
.Nm egghead tools mcp
.Cm add Ar name
.Op Fl -stdio Ar command | Fl -http Ar url
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A tool is a function the model can call.
.Nm
ships a built-in set
.Pq record-store tools, web fetch, filesystem, subprocess
and lets you extend the catalog by registering Model Context Protocol
servers. The two sources merge into one menu, and which entries an
agent sees on that menu depends on the capabilities the agent holds.
.Pp
.Cm tools
inspects that catalog from both directions: the
.Cm list
subcommand walks the menu top-down (every tool, optionally filtered to
one agent), and the
.Cm mcp
subcommands walk it from the server side (registered servers, their
.Sy requires:
sets, and the agents eligible to use them).
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "mcp available"
.It Cm list
Print the catalog, grouped by source. Tools the agent can use are
marked with a green dot; tools filtered out by the offering-time
gate are dimmed and marked with a hollow dot. Default when no
subcommand is given.
.It Cm mcp list
List configured MCP servers and their connection status.
.It Cm mcp available
List the curated registry of common servers
.Pq Exa, GitHub, Brave, Slack, the local filesystem server, Egghead itself .
Aliased as
.Cm mcp registry .
.It Cm mcp show Ar name
Show one server's configuration, the tools it advertises, and the
list of agents whose grants are a superset of its
.Sy requires: .
.It Cm mcp who Ar name
Print the agents eligible to use the named server, one per line.
The inverse of
.Cm tools list --agent .
.It Cm mcp add Ar name
Register an MCP server. With a flag, the launch command is
declared explicitly; without one, the wizard walks through the
curated registry.
.It Cm mcp remove Ar name
Stop the server process and remove the entry from configuration.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--source val"
.It Fl -agent Ar agent-id
Filter
.Cm list
to the tools one agent can actually call.
.It Fl -source Cm all | local | mcp
Restrict
.Cm list
to one source. Default:
.Cm all .
.It Fl -stdio Ar command
Declare an MCP server's launch command for stdio transport, for
.Cm mcp add .
.It Fl -http Ar url
Declare an MCP server's HTTP URL, for
.Cm mcp add .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show help.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
The catalog one agent can actually call:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead tools list --agent scout
.Ed
.Pp
Register a server from the curated registry:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead tools mcp add exa
.Ed
.Pp
Register a server by hand:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead tools mcp add weather --stdio "mcp-weather"
egghead tools mcp add api    --http  "https://api.example.com/mcp"
.Ed
.Pp
Diagnose why a tool is missing from an agent's menu:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
egghead tools mcp show exa     # what does exa require?
egghead tools mcp who exa      # which agents are eligible?
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr egghead-agents 1 ,
.Xr egghead-skills 1 ,
.Xr egghead-mcp 1 ,
.Xr egghead 1 ,
.Xr egghead 7
